{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791589764,"nonce":"gNFNZgOuPPF5LsuGkBjCFTmvIc0=","message":"Unblurred box shadows draw as of ce6b2dc. The bug was in the TypeGPU shadow shader (shaders/ui/shadow.ts), not in blinc_abi's display list. The quad now grows by max(spread, 0) + 1 as well as by the blur and the offsets. The outer branch no longer needs blur or spread. With no blur, edges are antialiased over a pixel (outer: clamp(0.5 - d, 0, 1); inset: clamp(0.5 + inner, 0, 1)). The outer spread radius follows CSS: r + s(1 + u^3) with u = min(r/s, 1) - 1 when s \u003e 0, else max(r + s, 0). tests/native-theme.mjs checks that 0 0 0 8px draws a ring with square corners on a square box and rounded corners on a rounded one, that 10px 10px 0 draws an offset copy, and that 0 14px 0 -4px draws a narrower band under the box. The theme-shape and mixed inset tests use unblurred outer layers again.","files":null}]}